      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix scheduled `var_prefill_length` to describe the current prefill iteration instead of the full original prompts. Match vLLM: accumulate `2 * prefix_length + chunk_length`, then divide the population variance by four. For prefixes `[4, 2]` and chunks `[1, 3]`, the result is `0.25`, independent of future prompt tokens.\n\nThree executable production lines. The existing accumulator, schema, and other counters are unchanged. No new tests or assertions are added; one existing mixed-batch fixture supplies the chunk lengths required by the fix.\n\n## Validation\n\n**Correctness (archived GPU implementation):** **7 baseline mismatches → 0 candidate mismatches** across 56 received prefill-containing records. Emitted-metric coverage for progressed chunks with multiple prefills and mixed batches with multiple prefills remains incomplete after ten attempts because of existing zero-timer suppression; that issue is deferred.\n\n**Performance:** **Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B**, one H100 PCIe 80 GB, BF16/TP1, exactly **8,192 input / 1,024 output tokens**, chunk size 512, overlap/mixed chunks/radix cache enabled, raw streaming completions. AIPerf 0.13.0; five paired rounds with rotated variant order. All **60 fresh-server runs** completed: **8,000 measured requests**, 3,280 excluded warmups, zero request errors, and zero FPM stream gaps.\n\n“New” is the per-iteration variance fix; “old” is the baseline with the existing KV-counter correction and full-prompt variance. Each is compared with its own FPM-disabled baseline. Positive means worse: throughput loss or latency increase; negative means improvement. Values are paired geometric effects, with pointwise **95% Student-t intervals** over five within-round log ratios (four degrees of freedom).\n\n| Concurrency | Metric | New FPM on/off overhead | Old FPM on/off overhead |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | Throughput loss | +0.313% [+0.232, +0.394] | +0.275% [+0.136, +0.414] |\n| 1 | TTFT p50 increase | +1.912% [+1.096, +2.735] | +1.932% [+1.147, +2.724] |\n| 1 | ITL p50 increase | +0.219% [+0.159, +0.279] | +0.137% [+0.043, +0.230] |\n| 32 | Throughput loss | +0.015% [-0.040, +0.070] | +0.026% [-0.066, +0.118] |\n| 32 | TTFT p50 increase | +0.631% [-0.729, +2.010] | +0.065% [-1.084, +1.229] |\n| 32 | ITL p50 increase | -0.012% [-0.148, +0.124] | -0.057% [-0.226, +0.113] |\n| 128 | Throughput loss | +0.018% [-0.114, +0.150] | +0.001% [-0.060, +0.063] |\n| 128 | TTFT p50 increase | -0.012% [-0.106, +0.083] | +0.130% [-0.176, +0.436] |\n| 128 | ITL p50 increase | -0.024% [-0.196, +0.147] | +0.155% [-0.072, +0.382] |\n\nBoth implementations show measurable FPM enablement cost at concurrency 1; all on/off intervals at concurrency 32 and 128 include zero. All direct new-on/old-on intervals also include zero, which does **not** establish equivalence. The concurrency-1 ITL ratio-of-ratios is **+0.082% [0.027%, 0.137%]**, one of 45 pointwise comparisons without multiplicity adjustment. All valid rounds were retained. GPU clocks were not locked and varied at higher concurrency; throughput includes fill/drain, TTFT includes queueing, and ITL p50 is the median of per-request mean decode latency.\n\nThese results compare archived baseline `9848e3fa` with candidate `d43f8851`, both derived from audited `968726f3`; they were not rerun on the PR's current upstream base. This is the Qwen3 variance campaign, separate from the earlier Qwen2.5-7B counter-fix campaign.\n\n**Existing native tests:** At commit `d2e1775c`, all 21 tests in `test_forward_pass_metrics.py` pass. All added regression tests and assertions were removed; the only test-file change supplies `extend_lens` in the existing mixed-batch fixture. `git diff --check` passed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38291531474](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38291531474)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38291531098](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38291531098)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38291531491](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38291531491)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
